\import \root.GeneralLinear[K := C.Complex, field := C.Algebra[].field, conjugation := linear_algebra.Hermitian[].Complex[].scalar, scalar := vector_bundles.Bundles[].Complex[].scalar, n := s] \as TargetGL;
\import \root.ComplexLinear[r := s] \as Target;
\structure Data: \Set := { apply: GL.Carrier -> TargetGL.Carrier };
\structure Laws[data: Data]: \Prop := {
  identity: data.apply GL.identity = TargetGL.identity,
  product: \forall (u, v: GL.Carrier) -> data.apply (GL.multiply u v) = TargetGL.multiply (data.apply u) (data.apply v),
  smooth: \forall (d: N.Nat^)(U: calculus.Real[].Multivariable[n := d].Open[].OpenSet)(f: calculus.Real[].Multivariable[n := d].Open[].Carrier U -> GL.Carrier) ->
    \root.ComplexLinear[r := r].Smooth[d := d].Regular U f -> Target.Smooth[d := d].Regular U (\fun (x: calculus.Real[].Multivariable[n := d].Open[].Carrier U) => data.apply (f x)),
};
\definition Representation: \Set := \Cast[Data] ({ data: Data \where Laws[data] });
\definition laws[representation: Representation]: Laws[representation] := \bysub(Data, Representation, representation);
